From 8fa8b1aceee3a1a4e135ebff5e2717ec0eaf6169 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joonhoekim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 01:30:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 48/56] leds: rgb: add Awinic AW22127 driver

The TB323FU rear-camera RGB ring. The AW22127 runs effects on an
internal MCU (program in its own flash). The driver sends it the
"all LEDs one colour, in steps" command the vendor stack uses, through
the TASK1 mailbox, and exposes the ring as one multicolor LED.

Each step of the command carries a duration, a start and an end
brightness and the colour; the MCU ramps within a step and loops over
the steps. The colour goes in at full intensity and the LED brightness
in the step levels, so the chip does the scaling and the hue holds at
low brightness. A hardware pattern (pattern trigger, hw_pattern)
becomes one step per tuple, so effects such as breathing run without
host writes. Sending a command restarts the MCU, so a command equal to
the running one is not sent again. Off holds the chip in reset.
