+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+
+=====================================
+Kernel driver for Awinic AW22127 LEDs
+=====================================
+
+The AW22127 runs its lighting effects on an internal MCU. The driver drives
+all LEDs as one multicolor LED: ``multi_intensity`` is the colour and
+``brightness`` scales it in the chip.
+
+Hardware pattern
+----------------
+
+With the ``pattern`` trigger, ``hw_pattern`` runs a brightness pattern on the
+MCU, without further writes from the host. It takes "brightness duration"
+pairs, as the software ``pattern`` does (see
+Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-trigger-pattern.txt). Each pair is
+one step: it lasts ``duration`` milliseconds (1-65535) and ramps linearly from
+its brightness to the brightness of the next pair; the last pair ramps to the
+first. Up to 16 pairs.
+
+The pattern repeats until it is cleared, so ``repeat`` must be -1. The colour
+is the ``multi_intensity`` at the time ``hw_pattern`` is written; a later
+``brightness`` or ``multi_intensity`` write replaces the pattern with a steady
+colour.
+
+Breathing with a 3 second cycle::
+
+    echo pattern > trigger
+    echo "0 1500 255 1500" > hw_pattern
+
+Fade in over 0.5 s, hold 1 s, fade out over 1 s, stay off for 0.5 s::
+
+    echo "0 500 255 1000 255 1000 0 500" > hw_pattern
